  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "9eXWGZSkUsIquYDE9C+w9NV+Qkw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:50.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The open-source toolchain for working with IFC files (BIM briefing):\n\n- **ifcopenshell** \u2014 \"what everyone uses\"; the core IFC library. Notably ships an MCP server (docs.ifcopenshell.org/ifcmcp.html), making IFC directly accessible to agents. Speckle partially uses it under the hood.\n- **bimserver** (opensourcebim/bimserver) \u2014 open-source BIM server\n- **Bonsai** \u2014 Blender plugin for BIM authoring/viewing (extensions.blender.org); with sample IFC files from buildingSMART's test suite\n- **ifc-bench** (huggingface.co/datasets/sylvainHellin/ifc-bench) \u2014 benchmark dataset for evaluating BIM comprehension in AI systems: curated IFC models with QA pairs across 4 complexity categories\n- **cobbie** (github.com/sylvainHellin/cobbie) \u2014 Code-Based BIM Information Extraction, same author\n\nPipeline-relevant contact: Peter Kombolschek (via Jakob) is releasing an open-source **IFC viewer and editor supporting 4D (time) and 5D (costs)**. A well-known Austrian architect who works on BIM norms \u2014 potentially both a tool source and a distribution channel.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:11:50.972556+00:00"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:50.000Z"
    }
  },
